{
  "_comment": "Header-guard table. Rule (RULES.md part F): normalise a header (lower case, every run of non-alphanumeric characters becomes one space, trim). A header whose normalised form equals a normalised TEMPLATE header always passes. Otherwise it is REFUSED when it contains any of the whole words cost, rate, postage, label, carrier, net, wholesale, negotiated, paid, invoice, buy (an optional plural s is allowed). The guard runs over every header of every sheet BEFORE anything is stored. A header that passes auto-maps to a money field only when it is an exact template money header, or it contains 'charged to' or 'billed to', or it contains the word customer together with one of charge, charges, charged, amount, fee, price, total; any other money-like header is left unmapped. The guard is best effort: no rule can prove that a number is customer-facing. HOSTILE BLOCK (group 'hostile', appended in the database hardening pass): headers written to get past the word list. Expected outcomes follow the same rule with these steps added before the word test: (1) Unicode compatibility normalisation (NFKC or NFKD) so fullwidth and styled letters become plain ones; (2) every invisible format character (zero-width space, non-joiner, joiner, soft hyphen, word joiner, left-to-right mark, byte order mark) and every combining mark is removed; (3) common Cyrillic and Greek look-alikes are folded to the Latin letter they imitate (or a header that mixes scripts is refused); (4) camelCase is split BEFORE lower-casing, so 'UPSCost' is 'ups cost' and 'FedEx' is 'fed ex' (a carrier brand is recognised in any of those spellings: ups, usps, fedex, dhl, ontrac, lasership); (5) a number on either end of a word is trimmed ('cost1'); (6) stems wholesale, negotiated, postage and invoice are refused inside a longer word; (7) a carrier brand (or 'carrier') beside a money word (charge, fee, amount, price, total, billed, cost, rate, paid) is refused unless the header contains customer, 'charged to' or 'billed to'; (8) a NON-EMPTY header that normalises to nothing (only invisible characters or punctuation: '#', '$', '...') is refused, because the 3PL can rename it, unless it is an exact template header. Every 'refuse' row of the block is an obfuscated or hidden cost header; every 'pass' row is harmless. The SQL backstop must agree on every row of the block (tests/db/adjustments-header-sql.test.ts); the TypeScript guard (src/lib/adjustments/header-guard.ts) is held to the same rows by tests/unit/adjustments-import.test.ts.",
